Kernir patch 0004: the 7zip reader decrypts 7zAES (AES-256 + SHA-256) folders and encrypted headers

Upstream: libarchive 3.8.10, libarchive/archive_read_support_format_7zip.c (setup_decode_folder,
seek_pack, extract_pack_stream, get_uncompressed_data, read_consume, ppmd_read, read_Folder,
read_data, cleanup). Needs include/kernir_7zaes.h and libarchive/kernir_7zaes.c (CommonCrypto).

Upstream stops at "The file content is encrypted, but currently not supported". Here each 7zAES
coder is a decryption stage on the packed stream it reads: setup_decode_folder() records the key
(from the first passphrase only, through a per-reader cache keyed on cost, salt and passphrase)
and IV per packed stream, then works on a copy of the folder without the AES coders, so
[AES, LZMA2] reads as [LZMA2] and the eight-coder BCJ2 form as the usual four-coder one
(read_Folder now accepts 8 coders and keeps the packed-stream map). seek_pack() starts
AES-256-CBC on an encrypted stream; extract_pack_stream() and ppmd_read() read it through a
decrypted buffer of 64 KiB plus one block, and the COPY fast path that hands out read-ahead
pointers is off for an encrypted folder. Messages: no passphrase gives "Passphrase required for
this entry" (ARCHIVE_FAILED, ARCHIVE_FATAL for the header); bad coder properties
"... 7zAES coder properties"; other crypto coders "Crypto codec not supported yet". A CRC
mismatch in an encrypted folder (a wrong passphrase on stored data) is ARCHIVE_FAILED, not a
warning. Keys are wiped with memset_s.

Apply from Sources/CLibArchive: patch -p1 < patches/0004-7zip-aes-read.patch

